    "physical_description": "Woman's longyi of weft ikat tie-dyed silk in twill weave. With yellow and red stripes with a series of floral sprays that would stand vertically when the cloth is worn. Weft-ikat zinme design. In a twill weft-faced weave. A tubular garment with one seam. When worn the spare material is lapped over to the left and tucked in at the waist forming a pleat. The striped section which forms the inside pleat of the longyi is not seen when worn.",
    "summary": null,
    "historical_context": "Made by the Indha of the Inle Lake area of Shan State.",
